---
import VitralLayout from '../../layouts/VitralLayout.astro';
---

<VitralLayout
  title="About testsite"
  description="A small personal project about clear, practical notes and honest how-to writing."
  bodyClass="home"
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>About testsite.</h1>
      <p>This is a personal project built as a clean, static place for practical notes. It is intentionally small.</p>
      <p>The focus is how-to content: one goal, one reusable action, one source, one check. If a note cannot be used again, it should be rewritten or deleted.</p>
      <p>The site is built with Astro, deployed to GitHub Pages, and kept close to plain HTML.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-alt">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="grid grid-2">
        <div class="card">
          <h2 class="card-title">What this is</h2>
          <p class="card-body">A public notebook for practical notes, reusable steps, and honest writing.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h2 class="card-title">What this is not</h2>
          <p class="card-body">Not a productivity brand, not a course, not a template store. No newsletter wall.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p class="card-body">You can reach the project maintainer through GitHub issues in this repository.</p>
      <p class="section-cta">
        <a href="https://github.com/ismaelmmachado/testsite" class="link-underline">github.com/ismaelmmachado/testsite -></a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</VitralLayout>
